id: fake-death
name: Fake Death
uaType: technical
prerequisite: Personality Score 4+, 2+ Bluff Skill Ranks
tpCost: 8
type: outOfSequence
actionCost: 0
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
usageLimit: 1/encounter
# "After receiving Damage from an Opponent's Attacking Maneuver, you may choose to be knocked Prone" - offered on a
# card of its own when the Damage is dealt (chat.mjs offerFakeDeath). Taken: Prone, and a Clash (Bluff vs Intuition)
# against each Opponent asked; each won, Hidden from them through Fake Death (hidden.mjs `via`). The Movement
# Maneuver, used while so Hidden, ends every one of them.
fakesDeath: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Out-of-Sequence, once an Encounter, on taking Damage from an Opponent's attack: Prone, and a Clash (Bluff vs
  Intuition) against every Opponent - each won, Hidden from them. The Movement Maneuver ends it.
text: >
  Fake Death: With a dramatic cry of defeat or a sudden stillness on the battlefield, you topple over pretending to
  have died. Those around you must carefully consider whether or not you have actually fallen in battle or are
  waiting for a specific moment in battle to take advantage of.
  –Ability Type: Technical
  –Prerequisites: Personality Score 4+, 2+ Bluff Skill Ranks
  –TP Cost: 8
  –KP Cost: 4(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Out-of-Sequence
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: After receiving Damage from an Opponent’s Attacking Maneuver, you may choose to be knocked Prone. If you
  do, make a Clash (Bluff vs Intuition) against all Opponents. If you win, you become Hidden to those Opponents.

  If you use the Movement Maneuver while Hidden through the effect of Fake Death, you stop being Hidden.

  You may only use this Unique Ability once per Combat Encounter.
